{# ============================================================================
   THE ROSTER AT ORGANIZATION SCOPE — the frame its three screens share.

   THE FRAME IS THE SHELL'S, WHOLE. The trail, the tab strip and the scope
   control are drawn by `@Shell/org_page.html.twig` from the same
   `orgPages()` declaration the sidebar row is mounted from — so a tab and a
   sidebar row cannot disagree about which screens this module has. This
   file used to draw the strip itself; two copies of one list is how they
   come to differ.

   WHAT IS LEFT HERE is what only this module can say: the sheet its own
   vocabulary lives in, and the sentence under the page title. There is no
   area anywhere in it, which is the whole difference from the area base —
   an organization-level screen is the area screen one scope wider.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@Shell/org_page.html.twig' %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {# The widget grid's sheet, for the surface the Overview composes. #}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\ShellBundle\\ShellBundle::WIDGET_STYLESHEET')) }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\UhifadhiRosterBundle::STYLESHEET')) }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Who is due, who checked in, and where their handset says they actually are &mdash; <b>{{ scope.isOrganization ? 'across every area' : scope.label }}</b>. The stations and the live positions are each area&rsquo;s.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}{% block roster_org_page %}{% endblock %}{% endblock %}
